      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1087",
      "html": "<ul><li>Scientific name: Lophiosilurus fowleri (Haseman, 1911)</li><li>Common names: Rusty Jelly Catfish, Orange Catfish, Oremon Catfish, Pocoma (Brazilian)</li><li>Type locality: Rio São Francisco, Cidade de Barra, Bahia, Brazil.</li><li>Synonyms: Cephalosilurus fowleri, Pseudopimelodus fowleri</li><li>Etymology: Greek, lophos = crest + Greek, silouros = cat fish -&gt; Crested catfish. Named for the prolific ichthyologist, Henry Fowler.</li><li>Identification: Larger and with a more orange colouration than C. apurensis.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1087",
      "html": "<p>South America: São Francisco River basin, Brazil.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1087",
      "html": "<p>Temperature: 23.0-27.0°C (73.4-80.6°F).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1087",
      "html": "<p>Caves, driftwood, sand, floating plants.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1087",
      "html": "<p>Fish (fresh and frozen), krill, shrimp, earthworms, mice, rats, sinking pellets, shrimp pellets, any \"meaty\" type foods with a little variety thrown in.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1087",
      "html": "<p>Very aggressive and not shy. Best kept alone or in the most bullish of considerably larger company.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1087",
      "html": "<p>Females larger and much more aggressive, very distinguishable dimorphism by venting especially at larger sizes.</p>"
    },
